{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1539097-dream-shenanigans-that-i-don-t-think-have-been-addressed","id":1539097,"title":"Dream shenanigans that I don't think have been addressed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-23T06:36:00-07:00","id":1539097,"title":"Dream shenanigans that I don't think have been addressed","content":"Is it even possible to find the Gate of Horn <i>from </i>the Dreaming Roads? What happens if you do?<br /> If you passed the Gate of Ivory, left your Bastion, and passed the Gate of Horn into the Hedge, what state would you be in? Could you then walk out of a normal Hedgeway into the &quot;real&quot; world? What state would you be in <i>then</i>?<br /> Is there a published answer? If there isn't, what do you think should happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T07:38:20-07:00","id":1539098,"title":"","content":"Navigating the Dreaming Roads works like navigating the Hedge except as noted (no Hedgespinning, everything that's not on the Roads or part of a Bastion's territory counts as Thorns, each Road counts as a 3-5 dot trod) and the Gate of Horn is both elusive and every entrance to the Dreaming Roads.<br /> <br /> The Dreamborn's existence as persistent beings allows them to exist in more dreams than the one that birthed them, but cannot leave their Bastion without a particular Numen and cannot leave the Dreaming Roads through the Gate of Horn even then, which would be an odd thing to specify if using the Gate of Horn as an exit was impossible (to say nothing of what that would imply for using it as an entrance).<br /> <br /> There is no state of Twilight in the Hedge and Hedge Ghosts need a Numen to dematerialize while there; the corebook's section on the Gate of Ivory specifies that lucid dreamers (including changelings) can't make the roll to wake up outside of their own dreams or the Dreaming Roads (needing to find the exit to anyone else's Bastion before they can make the roll), and specifically includes &quot;elsewhere in the Hedge&quot; in that external category, which would also be an odd thing to specify if it wasn't possible to leave through the Gate of Horn.<br /> <br /> There's no published answer for whether a projecting oneiropomp can leave the Hedge itself, though a character deposited in the mortal world from the collapse of a Bastion are in a state of Twilight (presumably the same mental frequency occupied by other forms of astral projection) and must find their way to their body and then make the roll to wake up; enough things in the Hedge cannot leave its boundaries (whether universally or conditionally) that you can decide whether or not a normal Hedgeway allows passage to dreaming characters on whatever consistent or selective basis suits the needs of your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T07:44:58-07:00","id":